# ai-config pre-scan ratchet baseline — issue #907.
#
# Findings from check-ai-config's deterministic pre-scan that exist in the
# tree TODAY. The scheduled job (.github/workflows/ai-config-prescan.yml)
# fails on any finding NOT listed here, so this file is what keeps it green
# on the current tree while still catching the next one.
#
# THESE ARE REAL FINDINGS, NOT FALSE POSITIVES. They are recorded as
# known-and-deferred: fixing them is per-skill prose work, deliberately out
# of scope for #907 (which is about making the cadence RUN). Removing an
# entry by fixing its file is always welcome — --regen then tightens the
# ratchet. ADDING an entry is a deliberate, reviewable diff that wants a
# reason in the commit message.
#
# Format: file<TAB>category<TAB>evidence  (no line number — it churns on
# unrelated edits and would report known findings as new).
#
# Regenerate with: bash bin/ai-config-prescan.sh --regen
